  <layout>One block of verse, one column, with a running head at the top; faint marginal show-through on the right side is not transcribed; a catchword "Et" at the lower right corner.</layout>
  <page_number />
  <running_head>THEOD. BEZÆ</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Et</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Tristes per Umbras ambiguis secant.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2" para="true">
      <i>Quotquot resurgens Sol renouat dies</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Cursu rotantur dissimili, pigras</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>Æstate ducunt frugifera moras:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">
      <i>Bruma rigentis temporibus statim</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6" para="true">
      <i>Volant recisi, mox niveo nitent</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Fulgore sudi, mox nigricantibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">
      <i>Velantur Umbris, mox rapido impigris</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Ardore messes agricolis coquunt,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10" para="true">
      <i>Mox cuncta inerti rura premunt gelu.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Nunc terra odoro multiplices sinu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12" para="true">
      <i>Flores refundit, quum placidus novo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">
      <i>Demulcet auras Vere Favonius,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>Latisque Vestit frondibus arbores.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Nunc squallet omnis, quum Boreas plaga</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16" para="true">
      <i>Frigus reducens Sarmatica ruit:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Quum sæva campos pallidulis hyems</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18" para="true">
      <i>Spargit pruinis, et nive candida.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">
      <i>Nec Vultus idem caruleis manet</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20" para="true">
      <i>Ubique ponti fluctibus: aut sua</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Feruente quassans littora murmure</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22" para="true">
      <i>Urbes propinquas territat, et satis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>Minatur agris diluuiem: aut Noto</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24" para="true">
      <i>Silente, et Eurus, atque Aquilonibus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Deponit iras littoribus suis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26" para="true">
      <i>Hærens quietus, nec Zephyro abnuit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27" para="true">
      <i>Leni pauentes tergore nautas.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28" para="true">
      <i>Non ille prudens qui dubiis Videt</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29" para="true">
      <i>Volui perorbem motibus omnia,</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Show-through from the facing page at the right margin; the catchword "Et" is partly cut off. Some letters in the Greek-style names (Zephyro, Vere) are uncertain; the long s is transcribed as s throughout. Line-initial capital letters with a decorative form, such as "Ʃ" and "Ṽ", are read as S and V.</notes>
</page>
